PART 1: THE GAP FUNCTION g(x) = x³ - x² - x - 1
------------------------------------------------------------

  φ (golden ratio)    = 1.6180339887
  τ (tribonacci)      = 1.8392867552
  2 (fugacity)        = 2

  g(φ) = -1.0000000000  (should be -1)
  g(τ) = 0.000000000000000  (should be 0)
  g(2) = 1.0000000000  (should be +1)

  ALGEBRAIC VERIFICATION:
  φ² = φ+1 = 2.6180339887, actual φ² = 2.6180339887
  φ³ = 2φ+1 = 4.2360679775, actual φ³ = 4.2360679775
  g(φ) = (2φ+1)-(φ+1)-φ-1 = -1  ✓

  COXETER CLASSIFICATION via g(x):
  g(x) < 0  ⟹  spherical type  (finite reflection group)
  g(x) = 0  ⟹  Euclidean type   (affine, flat)
  g(x) > 0  ⟹  hyperbolic type  (infinite, negatively curved)

  φ lives in spherical:   g(φ)=-1  (Fibonacci, finite geometries)
  τ is the flat boundary: g(τ)=0   (tribonacci, critical dimension)
  2 lives in hyperbolic:  g(2)=+1  (tournament fugacity, {3,∞})

  GAP VALUES AT NOTABLE CONSTANTS:
