PART 2: THE MODULAR GROUP AND TOURNAMENT OPERATIONS
------------------------------------------------------------

  PSL(2,Z) = ⟨S,T | S²=(ST)³=1⟩  (the modular group)

  TOURNAMENT INTERPRETATION:
    S  (order 2): complement T → T^c   [reversal involution]
    ST (order 3): 3-cycle rotation      [tournament atom]
    T  (order ∞): vertex addition        [growth operation]

  This is the (2,3,∞) triangle group, tiling the hyperbolic plane.
  The tessellation {3,∞} arises from the face (triangle) + vertex (∞).

  MODULAR FUNCTION CONNECTION:
    The j-function j(τ) = 1/q + 744 + 196884q + ...
    744 = 3 × 248 = 3 × dim(E₈)
    196884 = 196883 + 1  (monstrous moonshine)


PART 3: COMPATIBLE FRACTION → 1/e AND THE BRANCHING RATIO
------------------------------------------------------------

  For random tournament: E[H] = n!/2^{n-1}

  Compatible fraction = E[H]/n! = 1/2^{n-1}

    n= 2: E[H]/n! = 1/2^ 1 = 0.50000000   (ratio to 1/e = 1.359141)
    n= 3: E[H]/n! = 1/2^ 2 = 0.25000000   (ratio to 1/e = 0.679570)
    n= 4: E[H]/n! = 1/2^ 3 = 0.12500000   (ratio to 1/e = 0.339785)
    n= 5: E[H]/n! = 1/2^ 4 = 0.06250000   (ratio to 1/e = 0.169893)
    n= 6: E[H]/n! = 1/2^ 5 = 0.03125000   (ratio to 1/e = 0.084946)
    n= 7: E[H]/n! = 1/2^ 6 = 0.01562500   (ratio to 1/e = 0.042473)
    n= 8: E[H]/n! = 1/2^ 7 = 0.00781250   (ratio to 1/e = 0.021237)
    n= 9: E[H]/n! = 1/2^ 8 = 0.00390625   (ratio to 1/e = 0.010618)
    n=10: E[H]/n! = 1/2^ 9 = 0.00195312   (ratio to 1/e = 0.005309)
    n=11: E[H]/n! = 1/2^10 = 0.00097656   (ratio to 1/e = 0.002655)
    n=12: E[H]/n! = 1/2^11 = 0.00048828   (ratio to 1/e = 0.001327)
    n=13: E[H]/n! = 1/2^12 = 0.00024414   (ratio to 1/e = 0.000664)
    n=14: E[H]/n! = 1/2^13 = 0.00012207   (ratio to 1/e = 0.000332)
    n=15: E[H]/n! = 1/2^14 = 0.00006104   (ratio to 1/e = 0.000166)

  Note: 1/2^{n-1} → 0 as n → ∞
  But the per-arc branching factor is (n!/(n-1)!)^{1/(n-1)} / 2 = n^{1/(n-1)}/2

