PART 5: THE BINARY SKELETON AS {3,∞} GEOMETRY
------------------------------------------------------------

  26 BINARY PHENOMENA ↔ {3,∞} GEOMETRY:

  {3} face (triangle atom):
    • Ω girth ∈ {3,∞}        — triangle or nothing
    • H always odd            — Rédei = triangle parity
    • β₂ = 0 always           — triangles fill all 2-holes
    • H=7 impossible          — triangle overshoot
    • H mod 4 = 1+2α₁ mod 4  — triangle count controls mod-4

  {∞} vertex (unbounded valence):
    • β₁·β₃ = 0              — seesaw (infinite allocation)
    • Sharp thresholds        — each Betti number onsets at precise n
    • rank(d₂) ∈ {n-1,n}     — boundary saturates
    • SC vs non-SC dichotomy  — involution is total or absent

  {3,∞} interaction (finite face × infinite vertex):
    • K(n,2) girth transition — Petersen at boundary n=5
    • Permanent gaps {7,21}   — triangle × Hurwitz prime
    • Per-path identity fails — growth overwhelms atom at n=6
    • Pf classification       — Pfaffian correlates with homology


